note convert writes "Pling" if n is divisible by 3, then "Plang" if by 5, then "Plong" if by 7,
note or the decimal digits of n when it is divisible by none of them, into o; returns the length.
note Check it with: sh exercise.sh exercises/raindrops
om2
fn convert n ulong o edit uchar * to ulong
note replace this line with your solution
trap 13
end
